  "caption": "Quinn bought gorgeous pointy shoes, and by lunch the big toe was shouting. Cue a very dramatic search for 'bunion emergency'.\n\nA bunion is a gradual change in how the big toe joint lines up, not a growth. Genes play the biggest part, and the size of the bump often doesn't match how much it hurts.\n\nWhat often helps: shoes with a wide, deep toe box and modest heels, toe spacers or pads for comfort, and strength work for the big toe, arch and calves. Many people can keep running in a comfortable, roomy shoe. Night splints may feel nice, but they won't reshape the toe.\n\nIf foot pain is changing the way you walk, or the toes next door are getting sore, it's worth an assessment.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
